We are sorry that you had such bad luck with 1.4, but I don't think that
your bug reports are being ignored. We are working on fixing them, but
sometimes it is difficult to duplicate the bugs on different hardware.

For example I cannot run 1.4 either on two of my machines. One has
'we' cards and it panics just after it enables ipf, and the other is
a no name amd-k6 box and it just keeps rebooting at the second stage
boot blocks. Should I go remove that we support from the i386, when
it works on so many other machines.

| Of course, nobody can demand that you fix bugs unless they pay you to do so.
| But one can ask you not to claim support for machines where the current
| release just plain doesn't work.

